    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d65">

                <pb facs="0188" n="166" xml:id="pg166"/>

                <head>65. Memorandum From the President to the Secretary of State<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d65-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                ><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1961-05-27">May 27, 1961</date>.</hi></dateline></opener>
                <p>I am extremely anxious that we implement any promises that the Vice President may
                    have made in the various countries he visited during his recent trip. I would
                    appreciate it if you would put someone in charge to check on these promises and
                    send me a report on it after my return from Europe next week.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d65-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">John
                            Kennedy</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d65-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d65-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Conference Files: Lot 65 D 366, CF 1883. Attached to
                    a memorandum from G to S/O, June 1, which stated
                    that the President made a similar request to the Secretary of Defense and that
                    the Vice President made an oral request along these lines.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d65-f2" n="2" xml:id="d65-f2-content">
                <p>The President was in Vienna, June 3 for talks with Premier Khrushchev.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
